## What I checked

- Working tree is clean; `f6e442b` is the selective-rebuild work, which matches the board's newest **Closed** entry. Nothing is half-landed.
- Rename counts re-measured: **2,107 occurrences across 847 files**, of which **1,440 in 775 files** are `@udaan/`. The board says 2,024/1,430 — the gap is method, not drift (it summed `grep -c`, which counts *lines*; I used `grep -o`). Same picture.
- Board's two code citations are still correct: `payments.module.ts:56` binds `UnconfiguredPaymentProvider` on production, `notifications.module.ts:21` binds `LogNotificationProvider`. The board is current, not stale.
- Items 2 and 3 are as described: item 2's measured half is one deliberately-open judgement (item 17), one standing judgement (Best-margin rail), and a real touch device this sandbox cannot be; item 3 is five product decisions that each need an account or an owner.

## The one new finding

The three rename rows that need a yes/no are risky **only if something is actually deployed** — orphaned Cloud Run services, signed-out users, an old systemd timer. CLAUDE.md flags that "CI has never fired" became an assumption once a remote existed. I tried to settle it: **there is no `gh` and no `ssh` in this sandbox**, so run history and repository settings are unreadable from here. It cannot be settled without you. If nothing has been deployed yet, all three consequences are zero and item 1 collapses to one mechanical pass.

## To unblock item 1, I need four answers

| # | Question | Consequence of yes |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Casing: `Thok` in prose/UI, `thok` in identifiers and the `@thok/*` scope? | None — this is just following the existing convention |
| 2 | Session keys → `thok.session.v1` / `thok.admin.session.v1`? | Signs out every logged-in user across web, desk and the phone's SecureStore |
| 3 | `CLOUD_RUN_SERVICE_PREFIX` default `udaan` → `thok`? | Next deploy creates `thok-api-dev` *beside* a still-running `udaan-api-dev` and moves no traffic |
| 4 | `udaan-backup.{service,timer,cron}` → `thok-backup.*`? | Leaves the old timer running on any host that already has it installed |

Leave the `udaan-database-url-<env>` Secret Manager row **alone** unless you rename it in GCP first — the board is right that renaming it here makes the docs wrong rather than the deploy broken.

Two things to know before you answer 1: `TOTP_ISSUER` defaults to `Udaan`, so changing it re-labels every already-enrolled authenticator entry (the secret stays valid); and CLAUDE.md's own same-commit rule means its ~208 prose mentions move in the same pass, which is the judgement-heavy part rather than the sed.

Say the word on those four and I'll do the whole rename in one pass. If you'd rather I start with the fully-internal part — the `@thok/*` scope rename, seed accounts and the image label, none of which leaves the repo — I can do that now, but it leaves the name inconsistent in exactly the three places that matter operationally, which I'd rather not ship without you choosing it.

