💬 Done. Here's what happened.

## What I did

`plan.md` had four open items. Three (2, 3, 4) explicitly need a decision from outside the code — a revised `design.html`, a payment rail, a merge-or-close call on five Dependabot branches. **Item 5 was the only one this machine could answer itself**: the Udaan→Thok rename was never rendered.

Ran `tools/render/setup.sh` (~20 min: Chromium + an 81-package sysroot), then the harness over all three surfaces.

## Result: the rename moved nothing

**12 findings on the two clients, 0 on `apps/landing` — none of them new.** Ten are item (17)'s `.admin-desk-list__name` ellipsing; two are the standing Best-margin pair. Zero overflow, target-size, contrast, misaligned-row, empty-band or print findings. All four faces confirmed loaded, so fit results are exact — which was the whole question, since the strings changed length.

## Two things worth flagging

**The sweeps couldn't have answered the actual risk.** Item 5 pointed at the 236px rail, and the defect that box already produced (the third run's "Sign / out") is a *wrap* — neither clipped text nor horizontal overflow, so `checks.mjs` is blind to it by construction. I measured it directly: lockup reads `T`+`Thok`+`Ops`, every leaf one line, ~15px clear at both widths; `Sign out` is 63 × 44 on one line. The probe's first verdict was four false alarms (it inferred line count from box height, reading a 44px target as three lines) — caught by testing the check rather than reading it. Left in `/tmp`, not committed: `anchor-probe.mjs` pins a live rule, this answered a one-off.

**The board was wrong about one thing.** Item 5 called `Thok Ops तक पहुँच नहीं` "the one place the rename put Latin text inside Devanagari". It didn't — `git show 8832258^` has `Udaan Ops तक पहुँच नहीं` and three more. The mixed script predates the rename, which made it one character *shorter*. Corrected in place.

## Caveats I wrote down rather than hid

No run draws any Hindi at all (the harness seeds no locale), and `NoAccessScreen` — which holds that line — is drawn by nothing, being a cross-app guard refusal. Both are limits of the instrument; the direction of error is safe.

## Files touched

`CLAUDE.md` and `plan.md` only — no application code. Closed item 5 and moved it to § "Closed"; added the twenty-sixth-run entry; corrected a stale Part I count ("eleven browser runs" → twenty-six, with the defect tallies marked as floors since I couldn't verify them). `prettier --check` passes.

One incidental observation now in the board: item 5 was filed under "Open — each needs an answer this repository cannot give itself", and it was the one row there this repo *could* answer. A wrong row under a strong heading reads as blocked and doesn't get picked up.

I haven't committed — say the word and I will.

