💬 **Item 1 is done.** Item 2 I've stopped short of, deliberately — reasoning below.

## Item 1: "make redis url optional in development"

The premise needed checking first, and it turned out the literal reading was already true: `REDIS_URL` has been `.optional()` since it was added, `.env.example` ships it commented out, and `RedisService` is built `lazyConnect` precisely so an unset URL is survivable.

Where it was **still required** is a development *deployment*. The Cloud Run `dev` environment runs `NODE_ENV=production` on purpose — it's a real deployment, so it wants placeholder secrets refused and https demanded — and that one variable was also carrying "this is the production fleet", which is what the Redis check read. Net effect: dev owed a Memorystore instance and a VPC connector to pass a boot check, on the environment whose database had *just* been moved to Supabase specifically so dev needs nothing inside the project. Your `error.log` shows you're actively fighting that deploy.

So the fix splits the two facts rather than weakening the check:

- **`RATE_LIMIT_ALLOW_IN_PROCESS`** (default `false`) — a **permission, not a switch**. Nothing downstream reads it; `CommonModule` still picks its storage off `REDIS_URL` alone. Its only effect is that the production refusal stops firing. Setting it on a service that *has* Redis changes nothing.
- A `RateLimit` warning on every boot that exercises it, because the symptom — limits quietly worth `THROTTLE_LIMIT × instances` — is invisible from outside, and `/health/ready` won't even mention Redis (that indicator is only registered when the URL is set).

Four spec rows, each proved able to fail. The one that matters guards the tempting tidy-up: reading the flag at the storage line (`allowInProcess ? undefined : …`) reads like the same sentence and would silently turn off fleet-wide buckets on a service with a perfectly good Redis. That mutation fails exactly one row; every pre-existing row in the file passes straight through it.

Docs updated in the same change per the repo rule: `.env.example`, `docs/configuration.md` (table, rate-limiting section, Cloud Run secrets), `scaling.md`, `incident.md`, the workflow header and bootstrap summary, and CLAUDE.md.

**Gates:** typecheck, lint, `prettier --check`, build all pass. `npm test` green across all eight workspaces — api 1815 → 1819, exactly my four new rows. `npm run openapi` produces no diff (no contract changed). I did not run `tools/render` — no layout, token, or `desk.css` change. Nothing is committed yet.

